{%- comment -%}
  Cart icon + count.

  Rendered from TWO places and they must stay identical:
    1. sections/drip-header.liquid  — the initial page render
    2. sections/cart-icon-bubble.liquid — re-rendered by cart.js / cart-drawer.js
       through the Section Rendering API after every add-to-cart, which
       REPLACES the innerHTML of #cart-icon-bubble.

  That is why this is a snippet rather than inline markup: if the two diverged,
  the header would silently change appearance the first time someone added an
  item to their cart.

  The mockup shows the count even when the cart is empty ("0"), which is why
  this does not follow Dawn's `{% if cart != empty %}` guard.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- render 'icon-bag' -%}

<span class="drip-cart__count" aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>

<span class="visually-hidden">
  {{- 'sections.header.cart_count' | t: count: cart.item_count -}}
</span>
